  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1985-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Substitution gives \\(a^{9a}=(9a)^a.\\) Taking the positive \\(a\\)-th root yields \\(a^9=9a,\\) so \\(a^8=9.\\) Therefore \\(a=9^{\\frac{1}{8}}=3^{\\frac{1}{4}}=\\sqrt[4]{3}.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Substitute \\(b=9a\\) into \\(a^b=b^a\\)",
        "Because \\(a\\gt0,\\) take the \\(a\\)-th root and simplify"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
